    },
    "body": "The recurrent byte accumulator loses token order. Add a typed signed H4 prefix state whose two shared update operations are selected from actual generated training answers, and reuse the existing read/emit/stop transition and writer. The new contextual order/content gate passes 64/64 development answers and paths; retaining only final roots falls to 56/64. All 13,248 earlier retained outputs and 512 recurrent control traces remain identical.\n\nThis is finite operator selection and structural retrieval against supplied sequence keys. All development answer strings occur in training; semantic query formation, learned relevance, joint primitive credit and general prose remain unfinished. No model promotion. Canonical token identities remain separate from Hamming geometry. The byte adapter retains its previous reader; the prefix adapter shares its action/writer transition.\n\nValidation: optimized offline Rust build; one new focused arithmetic/corpus/bounds/identity test and 25 retained tests; actual output fit plus separately sealed evaluation resume with the identical candidate; boundary EOS and artifact reload/corruption checks; formatting, claim wording and diff checks. The first report stopped on a byte-only-dot boundary fixture outside the frozen policy's trained stopping context. The corrected span-context check reused the candidate without refitting or changing the data, gate or model source. Both reports and source/binary versions remain preserved.\n\nRecord the owner's OSPF analogy and statically verified SpiralCore negative-route cache as research: route availability/admission/freshness are separate from learned relevance. Update the canonical plan/current state toward learned contextual compatibility where exact sequence-key equality is insufficient. Existing artifacts and both original dirty checkouts remain unchanged; no external spending or cleanup.\n\nReferences #973 and #964. Queue status acknowledgements are not test results. Detailed source/artifact receipts and limits are in `docs/native_geometric_ordered_state_973.md` and its linked evidence.\n",
